  {
   "id": "L3ehcUo7kxsJ",
   "from": "Dennis Murphy",
   "author": "0c39e60ddb38622b",
   "date": "2012-10-25T20:44:53Z",
   "subject": "Re: confidence interval or prediction interval in stat_smooth?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Manuel:<div><br></div><div>It&#39;s a confidence band. Here&#39;s a toy example:</div><div><br></div><div><div>DF &lt;- data.frame(x = 1:10, y = 0.4 + 0.6 * (1:10) + rnorm(10, sd = 0.5))</div><div>m &lt;- lm(y ~ x, data = DF)</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>lmdata &lt;- data.frame(DF, predict(m, interval = &quot;confidence&quot;))</div><div><div>ggplot(lmdata, aes(x, y)) + </div><div>    geom_point() +</div><div>    geom_line(aes(y = lwr), color = &quot;red&quot;, linetype = &quot;dashed&quot;) +</div>\r\n<div>    geom_line(aes(y = upr), color = &quot;red&quot;, linetype = &quot;dashed&quot;) +</div><div>    geom_smooth(method = &quot;lm&quot;)</div></div><div><br></div><div>Dennis</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Thu, Oct 25, 2012 at 1:22 PM, Manuel Spínola <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mspin...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
